{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If</b> — Now I know that You are exalted and see the lowly; therefore I know: if I walk in the midst of trouble, I know that You will give me life. And how will You give me life? That You will send Your outstretched hand and save me." "<b>Despite my enemies</b> — Rabbi Moses said: 'even upon my enemies.' In my opinion: it is as it sounds, 'despite my enemies,' as though to anger them, and the meaning is against their will."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 138, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:02.010217480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}